:`shift_right . l:Vec(Sym), h:Sym, r:Vec(Sym)`\n`  |- ... : Tape ![{ ...body... }] fold ;`\n`languages/src/turing.rs:168-178`; <<#DCFCE7>>
note right
  The body is real, correct Rust and says exactly
  what the paper's helper says: push `h` onto the
  left context, take the first cell of `r` as the
  new head, or `Sym::Blank` if `r` is empty.
end note

split

  :**LANE 1 — the native `.eval()` path**; <<#E0E7FF>>
  :`generate_eval_method` walks `language.types`\n`macros/src/gen/native/eval.rs:336-346`; <<#DBEAFE>>
  if (does the OUTPUT category carry\na native Rust payload?) then (yes)
    :emit `eval` / `try_eval` /\n`try_fold_to_literal`; <<#DCFCE7>>
  else (**no** — `Tape` has\n`native_type: None`)
    :`continue` — the whole `Tape`\ncategory is SKIPPED; <<#FEE2E2>>
    :the `![{ ... }]` body is never\nemitted into `eval.rs`; <<#FEE2E2>>
