:**`Tape::shift_right` is an inert constructor.**\n`__is_fold_redex` is `false` for every op\n(`target/generated/turing/dovetail_report.rs:3923-3925`),\nso the extractor does not even prefer a moved tape\nover an unmoved one — `__weigh` is <latex>1.0</latex> everywhere; <<#FEE2E2>>
stop

note right
  CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly. Write <latex>\mathrm{SR}</latex> for the
  `shift_right` node. `D_q0_0` rewrites
  <latex>(q_0, \langle L \mid 0 \mid R\rangle)</latex> into
  <latex>(q_1, \mathrm{SR}(L, 1, R))</latex>, and that term is a
  normal form: the write survives only as an unevaluated
  helper node.
  **THE TAPE NEVER CHANGES AND THE HEAD NEVER MOVES.**
  Nothing is silently wrong — no rule fires that should not,
  and the report is honest. The helper simply has no
  reduction rule anywhere in the generated system.
end note

